@@ -0,0 +1,197 @@
+# Memory agent executor
+
+The built-in executor that carries out a memory agent's work: it runs the
+agent as a restricted loop over a model and a fixed set of tools, inside a
+sandbox the vault's own folders bound. It is the part that makes
+`memory-agent` a first-class agent rather than a picked model: the agent's
+`AGENTS.md` is the run's system text, its `mcp.json` servers and `skills/`
+are the run's tools, and the model route is internal and never shown in a
+dropdown.
+
+[internal/memagent](../../internal/memagent) is the whole of it. The
+registry beside it (`memory-agents.json`, [registry.go](../../internal/memagent/registry.go))
+says which agent carries out which role; this page is the run.
+
+## Responsibilities and boundaries
+
+| Part | Responsibility | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Dispatch | Which agent carries out a role, with which route and level, and what it is asked | `Dispatch`, `promptFor` in [dispatch.go](../../internal/memagent/dispatch.go) |
+| Loop | Ask the model, run the tools it asks for, hand the results back, stop at a final answer or a limit | `Run`, `loop`, `runCall` in [loop.go](../../internal/memagent/loop.go) |
+| Tools | The memory server's four, the vault's three, the run's own two, then the agent's servers' | `toolsFor`, `memoryTools`, `vaultTools`, `scratchTools` in [tools.go](../../internal/memagent/tools.go) |
+| Sandbox | Which vault paths a run reads and writes, and nothing else | `Sandbox`, `Readable`, `Writable` in [sandbox.go](../../internal/memagent/sandbox.go) |
+| Scratch | The run's own folder, and the cache's 20 MB ceiling | `Scratch`, `GC`, `Cap` in [scratch.go](../../internal/memagent/scratch.go) |
+| Progress | What the window polls while a run goes, and the last run of each role | `StatusOf`, `begin`, `end` in [state.go](../../internal/memagent/state.go) |
+| Agent home | The agent's `AGENTS.md`, `mcp.json` and `skills/` | `LoadHome`, `Home.System` in [home.go](../../internal/memagent/home.go) |
+| MCP client | A server's tools, named `<server>__<tool>`, spoken to over stdio or streamable http | `openMCP`, `mcpTools` in [mcp.go](../../internal/memagent/mcp.go) |
+| Gateway | A turn sent through magpie's own gateway as an agent's request | `GatewayAsk` in [gateway.go](../../internal/memagent/gateway.go) |
+| Input | The conversations a learn run reads, the notes a dream or organize run dreams across | `Conversations`, `Notes` in [collect.go](../../internal/memagent/collect.go) |
+
+Not its business: the registry's CRUD (registry.go), the Memory tab and its
+routes (internal/gui), memory's store and lock (internal/memory), the
+gateway's routing (internal/gateway). The executor reads memory through
+`memory.Search`/`Save`/`Forget`/`Edit`, so the store's own lock, origin rules
+and last-good generation apply as they do to an agent's MCP calls.
+
+## Runtime path
+
+1. `Dispatch` loads `memory-agents.json` and takes the agent named, else the
+   role's default (`Registry.Default`). A role with no agent, or an agent of
+   another role, is refused: a run is never made up from defaults nobody
+   chose. The entry's `model` and `effort` are the route, unless the caller
+   names others.
+2. It builds the prompt from what the run was given (`Conversation`s,
+   `Note`s, scopes), cut to `MaxPrompt`, in words that name neither magpie
+   nor a vendor.
+3. `Run` takes the one-run lock — a slot in this process and the
+   `memory-agent.run` file across magpies — opens the vault, makes the run's
+   scratch folder, reads the agent's home and opens its MCP servers.
+4. The loop asks the model (`Ask`; the GUI wires `GatewayAsk`), runs each
+   call, and appends an assistant `tool_use` message and a user
+   `tool_result` message. A turn with no calls ends the run.
+5. `end` records the phase, the counts and the error, keeps the last run of
+   the role in `memory-agent-runs.json`, and the scratch folder is dropped
+   and the cache swept (`GC`).
+
+## Sandbox
+
+A run reaches the vault through `os.OpenRoot`, so a name that leaves the
+vault is refused by the kernel, and every component of a name is checked for
+a link first, so a link that stays inside the vault is refused too. On top of
+that:
+
+- **Read** `wiki/ inspirations/ memories/`; **write** `inspirations/
+  _digests/ candidates/ dreams/ logs/`. The vault's own record
+  (`.fish-import.json`), `credentials/`, `tmp/` and everything outside the
+  vault are never reached.
+- An absolute path, a Windows drive or UNC path, `..`, an empty name, and a
+  name with a link in it are `ErrOutside`. The allowlist is matched as
+  written: on Windows `WIKI` is the same folder as `wiki`, so letting a case
+  variant through would let a folder a run may not read through with it.
+- A note over `MaxReadFile` (4 MB) isn't read; a note over `MaxWriteFile`
+  (1 MB), or a run over `MaxWritten` (8 MB), isn't written. A listing gives
+  at most `MaxListed` entries and never a link.
+- A note is written beside itself and renamed over, so a run cut off halfway
+  leaves the note it had, never half of a new one.
+- Memories are read and written through the memory tools alone, which keep
+  memory's own lock and the rule that an agent's save never changes what the
+  user wrote.
+
+## Scratch and GC
+
+`<cache>/memory-agent/work/<run-id>/`, one folder per run, dropped when the
+run ends. A folder already there is taken only when it is a folder of its
+own: a link or a junction is refused, because every write would then go
+somewhere else.
+
+`GC` drops the oldest runs' folders until the space holds at most `Cap`
+(20 MB), and only ever a whole folder whose name is a run id under a
+`memory-agent/work` root: a root that isn't that shape is refused, so the
+vault, memories and magpie's other folders can't be reached by it. A link
+or junction is never weighed through nor followed: `WalkDir` reports one as
+no folder, so what it points at isn't walked and its own size is nothing,
+and `RemoveAll` drops the link itself. The run going is protected by the
+name of **its own folder** (`RunningScratch`, `"<role>-<time>"`), not by its
+role: a role names no folder, and a sweep told one would protect nothing.
+
+## Loop limits
+
+`MaxSteps` (40) ends a model that keeps calling tools; `RunTimeout` (20 min)
+ends a run that takes too long; `TurnTimeout` (5 min) bounds one request.
+`Stop` cancels the run going — its products stand, its phase is `stopped`,
+and it isn't an error; the flag is cleared when the next run binds, so a
+later run's own timeout isn't read as a stop. A tool that fails, a tool that
+**panics**, and a server that won't start, are tool errors the model sees
+(`is_error`), never a run that ends: a run starts from magpie's own backend,
+so a panic left to unwind would end every agent's gateway. The run's
+transcript says which server didn't start and why, and is bounded
+(`maxMessages`, 2000 characters a line).
+
+## State
+
+| Where | Holds |
+| --- | --- |
+| `memory-agent-runs.json` | Each role's last run: agent, model, start, end, phase, steps, notes written, memories saved, error. Written through temp-and-rename under a file lock, with `lastgood` keeping the last good generation. |
+| `memory-agent.run` | The one-run lock across magpies. |
+| In memory | The run going: phase, step of `MaxSteps`, and the last `maxMessages` transcript lines. Kept for the window after it ends, until the next run of that role. |
+| `<cache>/memory-agent/work/<run-id>/` | The run's own files, for what is too big for a conversation. |
+| `memory-audit.jsonl` | Every change a run made to memory: `{at, action, id, role, agent, result, scope, kind, error}`. |
+| `<vault>/logs/memory-conflicts.md` | Each machine change refused because the memory is the user's. |
+
+`StatusOf(role)` answers `{running, phase, doing, of, steps, wrote, saved,
+started, ended, messages[], error}` — what the GUI's status route and the
+Obsidian plugin poll.
+
+## Audit and conflicts
+
+Every change a run makes to memory is one line of
+`memory-audit.jsonl` (`LogAudit`), appended and flushed, never rewritten:
+`save`, `forget`, `remove`, `promote` and `status`, with the memory's id,
+the role, the agent, what it did (`added`, `merged`, `changed`, `forgotten`,
+`removed`, `promoted`, a new status, `refused` or `conflict`) and, when it
+didn't go through, why (`error`). A line holds no memory text — only what
+changed — so a secret in a memory never reaches the log, and one over
+`MaxAuditLine` is cut rather than written whole. A log that can't be written
+is noted with `log.Printf` and otherwise passed over: audit never stops a
+change the user asked for. Lines are appended one write at a time
+(`auditMu`), so two runs' lines are two whole lines.
+
+A machine change to what the user wrote is refused (`ConflictError`,
+`IsConflict`), and the refusal is added to `<vault>/logs/memory-conflicts.md`
+through the run's sandbox, so it is inside the folders a run may write and
+nowhere else: the memory's id, the action, the role, why it was refused
+(`origin=user`, `edited by the user`, or both) and the user's words, with
+one that looks like a secret replaced by `[redacted]`. The note is only ever
+added to (`Sandbox.Append`), and the memory itself is left exactly as it
+was — the tools check `memory.Get` before `Edit`/`Forget`/`Remove`. A change
+that leaves the user's words alone is not a conflict: a run may still save
+what is new, and forget what isn't theirs. `memory_status` is the machine's
+for a candidate it proposed; taking the user's own memory out of use is
+refused.
+
+## Failure and compatibility
+
+- An unreadable `memory-agents.json` runs nothing (the registry's rule); an
+  unreadable `AGENTS.md` or `mcp.json` ends the run before the model is
+  asked, so a run is never given other instructions than the ones written.
+- A missing `memory-agent/` folder is an empty home, not an error: a run
+  still has the memory tools and the vault.
+- A missing or broken `memory-agent-runs.json` reads as no last run, never as
+  a run that failed; its last good copy is read instead when there is one.
+- `sse` MCP servers are refused at load: a run speaks stdio and streamable
+  http only.
+- The prompts name neither magpie nor any vendor: they go to the model's
+  vendor as written.
+
+## Verification
+
+```sh
+go test ./internal/memagent -count=1
+go vet ./internal/memagent
+gofmt -l internal/memagent
+```
+
+The sandbox, GC, loop, MCP and gateway tests are the ones that matter:
+`TestSandboxRefusesOutside`, `TestSandboxRefusesLinks`,
+`TestSandboxWriteBounds`, `TestGCDropsTheOldestToTheCap`,
+`TestGCLeavesOtherFoldersAlone`, `TestRunLoopsUntilTheModelStops`,
+`TestRunEndsAtTheStepLimit`, `TestStopEndsTheRun`, `TestOneRunAtATime`,
+`TestMCPToolsAreGivenAndCalled`, `TestMCPFailuresAreToolErrors`,
+`TestGatewayAskSendsAndReads`, `TestConversationsLeavesTheListingAlone`.
+
+The `qa_probe_*` tests are the acceptance of these guarantees, one per
+risk:
+
+| Risk | Test |
+| --- | --- |
+| every shape of path against every folder | `TestQASandboxPathMatrix`, `TestQASandboxListingMatrix` |
+| a link anywhere, inside the vault or not | `TestQASandboxLinkMatrix` (`qa_probe_sandbox_test.go`) |
+| the write budget, and a refused write | `TestQASandboxWriteBudget` |
+| a run's folder that is a junction | `TestQAScratchFolderIsNotALink` |
+| the sweep's cap, order and whole folders | `TestQAGCPressure`, `TestQAGCTwiceDropsNothingMore` |
+| the run going is never swept | `TestQAGCKeepNamesTheRunGoing`, `TestRunningScratchIsTheRunsFolder` |
+| a junction is neither followed nor weighed through | `TestQADirSizeDoesNotCountThroughAJunction` |
+| a tool that panics, or hangs | `TestQAToolPanicDoesNotEndTheProcess`, `TestQALoopEndsAToolThatHangs` |
+| a failure, a cancellation, a stop, and the next run | `TestQALoopFailureLeavesNoState`, `TestQALoopCancellation`, `TestQAStopIsNotCarriedToTheNextRun` |
+| many runs asked for at once | `TestQALoopConcurrentAsks` |
+| the transcript stays bounded | `TestQALoopTranscriptIsBounded` |
