+## FISH Dock shared vault
+
+In the Dock build, a verified `.fish-import.json` at
+`<config>/knowledge/github-capability-vault` selects an independent Obsidian
+vault. Short memories move once to its `memories` directory, under the same
+native file lock; the entire former store and any journal are copied before an
+atomic publish. The original store remains a recovery copy. Legacy JSON keeps
+its existing migration and `.migrated` backup. A corrupt import marker or partial
+target is an error, never an empty store. GUI, CLI and independent MCP processes
+resolve this from their portable config directory, not an inherited environment
+variable (`memory.prepareFishMemory`, `TestFishVaultKeepsNativeMemoryAndOriginalCopy`).
+
+Long Markdown notes remain in their original relative folders. `fishvault.Search`
+reads them on explicit local searches, without model calls, with OS-root-confined
+paths and no links outside the vault. Hidden/config/credential/transaction folders
+and the native memories directory are excluded. Hits carry title, path, a bounded
+reference excerpt and an Obsidian URI; skipped oversized notes are counted.
+`memory_search` adds these global reference notes only without project/kind/tag
+filters. Save and forget still act exclusively on native short memories.
+
+The Memory tab exposes the vault and note search through its existing read route.
+A dedicated desktop Obsidian plugin uses three `/api/fish-vault/` routes for models,
+search and streaming chat. In addition to normal web authentication these require
+a separate private pairing token from a file outside the vault and a local,
+non-browser request. The Dock embed proxy cannot supply that token. Chat goes
+through the actual gateway handler as Obsidian, preserving routing, privacy,
+usage and cancellation. It never receives provider credentials. The plugin
+sends selected content only on user action; generated text is not written back
+to an existing note automatically (`TestFishVaultDesktopRoutesRequirePrivateTokenNotJustAdminCookie`).
+
 ## Source of truth
 
 The `memory` folder in magpie's config folder, one Markdown file per memory
